Description: native GNOME app that turns documents into a cited wiki
 gknowledge collects documents, notes and links (Markdown, text, PDF,
 HTML, EPUB) and turns them into a linked Markdown wiki in which every
 page records its sources. Questions are answered from the wiki with
 numbered citations that link back to the pages they came from.
 .
 The knowledge base is a plain folder of Markdown files with wikilinks
 and front matter, so it can be opened in other editors or kept in git.
 .
 It works fully offline with a built-in heuristic engine. Optionally it
 can use a local model through Ollama or LM Studio, any OpenAI-compatible
 endpoint, or the user's own ChatGPT plan. The gknowledge-mcp command
 exposes the wiki to MCP clients such as coding agents.
